# TypeScript file naming

Name files after their primary responsibility. Use a descriptive subject plus a role suffix:

- `*.model.ts` — domain data shapes and related types
- `*.types.ts` — shared or infrastructure type aliases
- `*.util.ts` — small pure utilities
- `*.validator.ts` — input or domain validation
- `*.service.ts` — side-effecting application or integration service
- `*.store.ts` — stateful store
- `*.handler.ts` — request, event, or command handler
- `*.schema.ts` — runtime schema definitions
- `*.config.ts` — configuration and providers
- `*.routes.ts` — route registration
- `*.component.ts` — UI component class
- `*.spec.ts` or `*.test.ts` — tests

Keep one primary responsibility per file. Do not create a suffix-only file for a single trivial declaration; use the smallest clear structure that matches the repository.
